    "title": "Man on moped killed on City Island Bridge: police - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Spencer Gustafson ,\n5 hours ago\nCITY ISLAND, The Bronx (PIX11) — A man was killed on Wednesday afternoon on the City Island Bridge, according to police.\nThe accident occurred when a man, 59, operating a moped heading south on the bridge and crossed over into the northbound lane at around 3:30 p.m. on Wednesday.\nMore Local News A Nissan, driven by a 38-year-old man, struck the moped driver, causing serious injuries throughout his body, officials said. The moped driver was taken to a local hospital, where he was pronounced dead.\nThe Nissan driver remained on the scene and was not injured, according to police.\nThe crash is under investigation.\nSpencer Gustafson is a digital content producer from Long Island who has covered New York state and city news since 2023. See more of his work here .\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to PIX11.\n3",
